WEBVTT

00:00:00.407 --> 00:00:10.517
In this video, you will add an event to the map, like a tree lighting, a market, a parade, or a haunted house, so families across Southern California can find it.

00:00:10.517 --> 00:00:14.838
You need to be signed in to add an event, and in this video we already are.

00:00:14.838 --> 00:00:15.814
We start on the map.

00:00:16.786 --> 00:00:18.460
Start at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:21.293 --> 00:00:23.843
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:25.515 --> 00:00:26.495
Then tap Allow.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:33.377
Now look at the top of the map, beside the search box.

00:00:33.377 --> 00:00:36.160
See your picture, or your initial, in a circle?

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:40.723
That is your account menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:40.723 --> 00:00:41.424
Tap it.

00:00:43.985 --> 00:00:46.984
In the menu, tap Add an event, home or contest.

00:00:49.605 --> 00:00:54.358
That is where you add anything new: an event, a contest, or your own home.

00:00:54.358 --> 00:00:55.530
Now tap An event.

00:00:57.304 --> 00:01:05.398
Events are for things the whole community can attend, like a tree lighting, a holiday parade, a market, or a haunted house.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:08.697
The first question is whether your event has a web page.

00:01:08.697 --> 00:01:11.058
If it does, paste the address here.

00:01:11.058 --> 00:01:18.032
When the page mentions your event's name and date, your event is marked Confirmed on the map, which people trust more.

00:01:18.032 --> 00:01:22.108
If you do not have one, tap No, Next, and the event still goes on the map.

00:01:23.868 --> 00:01:26.760
Type the event's name, the way people know it.

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:30.514
Then choose the season it belongs to, and the type of event.

00:01:30.514 --> 00:01:33.216
That is how visitors find it when they filter the map.

00:01:35.251 --> 00:01:36.933
Pick the first and last day.

00:01:36.933 --> 00:01:39.666
For a one-day event, pick the same day twice.

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:40.749
Then tap Next.

00:01:42.401 --> 00:01:44.318
Is it free to attend, or paid?

00:01:44.318 --> 00:01:46.792
Families plan around this, so say it clearly.

00:01:46.792 --> 00:01:48.093
Tap Free, then Next.

00:01:50.374 --> 00:01:51.314
Now where.

00:01:51.314 --> 00:01:54.784
Type the name of the place, the city, and the street address.

00:01:54.784 --> 00:01:59.635
The street address puts a pin in the right spot on the map, so families can get directions.

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:04.012
Describe it in a sentence or two.

00:02:04.012 --> 00:02:05.997
What will families see and do?

00:02:05.997 --> 00:02:08.937
That is the text people read before they decide to come.

00:02:11.987 --> 00:02:13.834
Last, check everything.

00:02:13.834 --> 00:02:16.335
You can change any line with its Edit link.

00:02:16.335 --> 00:02:18.934
Below that, Make it stand out is optional.

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:22.665
You can pick a Featured plan, or just list your event for free.

00:02:22.665 --> 00:02:25.433
Nothing is public until you tap Add my event.

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:29.028
Your event then goes on the map.

00:02:29.913 --> 00:02:31.547
Next up: Show off your home.
